## AI coding assistants

```bash
{{.BinaryName}} setup claude      # Register plugin with Claude Code
{{.BinaryName}} setup cursor      # Write .cursor/rules/{{.BinaryName}}.mdc
{{.BinaryName}} setup windsurf    # Write .windsurf/rules/{{.BinaryName}}.md
{{.BinaryName}} setup copilot     # Add a {{.PrettyName}} section to .github/copilot-instructions.md
{{.BinaryName}} setup gemini      # Add a {{.PrettyName}} section to GEMINI.md
{{.BinaryName}} setup codex       # Add a {{.PrettyName}} section to AGENTS.md
```

Every command except `setup claude` writes into the current project directory, so
run these commands from the root of the project the assistant works in. Re-run
them after every upgrade: `setup cursor` and `setup windsurf` overwrite their rule
file, while `setup copilot`, `setup gemini` and `setup codex` keep the existing
content of their file and replace only the {{.PrettyName}} section instead of adding a
duplicate.
